ng late LiPetri debate or fundraising stretch could narrow the margin enough to move this toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom Suozzi (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Tom Suozzi, the Democratic incumbent in a swingy Long Island district that Donald Trump carried in 2024, faces a rematch against Republican Mike LiPetri. Suozzi has built a dominant financial position, with about $5.7 million on hand to LiPetri's $0.7 million, and has picked up police and firefighter union endorsements even as a Trump-linked super PAC spends heavily against him. Most expert raters place the race at Likely D, though a few see it as Lean D, and prediction markets give Suozzi roughly a 90% chance. No public general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, ratings, and money. The race is rated Likely Democratic, with Suozzi favored by a mid-single-digit to low-double-digit margin and meaningful residual uncertainty given the district's swing nature and outside spending.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8709, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8955, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9213, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9012, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8932, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8983, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8878, "mar